    "finding": "The introductory modern-Korean distribution statement explicitly distinguishes 마다 from 은/는/도: it can co-occur with subject/object/genitive particles and precede adverbial case particles. 사람마다의 is an original modern example. This is directly applicable modern distribution evidence, separately from the later historical analysis.",
    "limits": "Only 마다 + 에 structural recovery is implemented for COV-018l. No contextual distributive-sense selection, unrestricted particle order, arbitrary historical/region forms or all adverbial-case followers are inferred. The earlier Yoo 2007 full distribution and 2018 regional comparison remain unreviewed; this new modern claim does not pretend to retrieve them."
